**(a) Functions of a graphic card (2 marks).** A graphic card (video card) is an expansion card with its own processor (GPU) and memory (video RAM). Its functions are:

- to **process the graphics data** sent by the CPU (images, video, 3-D and game graphics) and **convert it into the signals** that the monitor can display, so relieving the CPU of this work;
- to **store the image being displayed** in its video memory and to control the resolution, the number of colours and the refresh rate;
- to provide the **output ports** (HDMI, VGA, DisplayPort) that connect the monitor.

**(b) Role of firmware (2 marks).** Firmware is **permanent software stored in a ROM or flash memory chip inside a hardware device** (for example the BIOS/UEFI of the motherboard, or the program of a printer or router). It contains the **basic instructions that start the device and control its hardware**: on a computer the BIOS carries out the power-on self-test and loads the operating system, and in a device it provides the low-level control of its functions. It keeps its contents when the power is off and can be updated by "flashing".

**(c) Device controller (2 marks).** A device controller is an **electronic circuit (a chip or card) that controls a peripheral device and acts as the interface between that device and the CPU/memory**. It receives commands from the processor, operates the device, handles the transfer of data (with a buffer) and reports errors and status. *Examples (any one):* disk controller (hard disk), USB controller, network interface card, graphics controller, keyboard controller.
